-- title:
--   Good points of the two-chart model read unique non-node places
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, and $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Two geometric function fields occur: $\bar F_0 :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, and $\bar F :=$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction `ZMod.unitsMap` of unit groups attached to $q \mid q^2M'$; the hypothesis `hle` asserts $\bar F_0 \le \bar F$. On the residue side one has the level-$M'$ field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` and the level-$(q^2M', \mathrm{levelH})$ field `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over the residue field of $A$.
--
--   The finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen _ M')` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of $j$ for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve with that $j$-invariant has trivial $q$-torsion.
--
--   The datum `R₀` is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\bar F_0$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\bar F_0$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the level-$M'$ field over `ResidueField A` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ on the constants (`algebraMap_mem_iff`) and the residue map of $A$ on them, satisfying the scaling condition `exists_smul_mem`, and carrying a map `placeMap` on places which preserves degrees and is compatible with push-forward of divisors of non-zero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that `R₀` computes coefficientwise reduction: whenever a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ has image in $\bar F_0$, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀`-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Further fixed data: an index $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of $\bar F$ indexed by $W$. The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, identifying $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty) :=$ `OIg (lineInfty q)` as the Gauss ring, $f$ belonging to it exactly when $f \cdot y = x$ for Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ of non-zero reduction; `hIg`, that every line $\ell$ is $\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma \cdot \infty$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pull-back of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that pull-back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ permutes the family. The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ induces exactly $A$ on the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hSS_over`, that for $f \in$ `R₀.integers` which is regular at every place of $\bar F_0$ at which the base-changed $j$-expansion `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` is regular, and whose `R₀`-residue is $s$-integral, the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of that `R₀`-residue the difference $f - a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, invariance of each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ under pull-back along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, existence for each $s$ of $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $t - a$ a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$. Finally $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $\bar F$ to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (a valuation subring with surjective residue map of kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ and its residue map on constants, and satisfying `exists_smul_mem`), with `hR` asserting $R.\mathrm{integers} = O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ and `hR₀O` asserting that $f \in$ `R₀.integers` precisely when its image in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   Uniformiser and base-field data: an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), henselian (`hhens`), with algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$ (`hκ`). An auxiliary prime $\ell$ is given with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$, together with $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Lastly $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (`hA₁`), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for the algebra structure on $\bar F$ over $k_0$ obtained by composing $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$. It asserts: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\bar F / k_0$ such that (a) the compositum of $F_0$ with $k_0$-adjoining the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\bar F$, (b) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, (c) for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every family $a$ of elements of $T' :=$ `adjoin k₀ (image of K' in F̄) ⊔ F₀` with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$, and (d) every element of $\bar F$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients lies in $F_0$; for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1 :=$ `adjoin k₀ (image of K₁ in F̄) ⊔ F₀` whose structure map agrees on $A_1$ with the inclusion $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \bar F$; for every $j_1 \in T_1$ which in $\bar F$ is the image of the base-changed $j$-expansion `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq`, with $j_1 \ne 0$; and for every finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from the reduced level-$M'$ field to the reduced level-$(q^2M', \mathrm{levelH})$ field such that $R$-reduction of the image of any $f \in$ `R₀.integers` equals $j$ applied to its `R₀`-reduction, and such that $Q \in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ holds exactly when for some $s \in W$ a function $g$ is $s$-integral if and only if $j(g)$ is $Q$-integral — the three statements below hold for the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X_1 :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` and $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf`, whose chart algebras consist of the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$, respectively over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$.
--
--   The following local notions are used. For $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in T_1$: `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of either chart mapping to $x$ there are chart-algebra elements $g, h$ with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$, i.e. $f$ lies in the local ring of each chart at $x$; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$, i.e. $f$ lies in the maximal ideal. For a place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational and that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` is $P$-integral with $P$-value in $A$, that value having $A$-valuation $< 1$ exactly when `InMax x f`; this abbreviation is introduced alongside the others and does not occur in the conclusion. Next, `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of: the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ sends $x$ to the closed point; $x$ specialises only to itself; for every chart point $y$ over $x$ (on either chart) every chart-algebra element whose image in $\bar F$ is a non-unit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y$; and for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi($`jChartFin`$)$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`. Further, `Reads x Q` says that for every $f$ with `InStalk x f` the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue is $Q$-integral, and that residue is a non-unit of the valuation subring of $Q$ exactly when `InMax x f`. Finally, `OffBranch x` says that for every line $\ell \ne$ `lineInfty q` and every chart point $y$ over $x$ (on either chart) there is a chart-algebra element which is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and does not lie in $y$.
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of three assertions. First, for every $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x`: there exists a place $Q$ with `Reads x Q`; any two places read by $x$ coincide; and every place read by $x$ lies outside $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. Second, for all $x, x' \in \mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x` and `GoodPt x'`, if some single place $Q$ is read by both then $x = x'$. Third, for every place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` with $Q \notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ there exists $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x`, `OffBranch x` and `Reads x Q`.
--
--   This is the point-place dictionary for the $\infty$-Igusa component of the two-chart integral model: good closed points of the special fibre lying on that component, away from supersingular $j$-invariants, correspond bijectively to the places of the reduced level-$(q^2M', \mathrm{levelH})$ function field that are not Igusa nodes, and the point produced for a given non-node place can be taken off all other Igusa branches. The three conjuncts assemble the existence, uniqueness, non-node, injectivity and surjectivity statements proved separately, and the result is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks) to organise the residue discs of the smooth Igusa base model.
